  "prefLabel": "Frl 403.05 Reinstatement",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Frl 403.05 Reinstatement. Any individual desiring reinstatement of their license shall show evidence of completion of at least the following minimum CE credits:\n\n(a) Individuals who have not held an active license for 3 months or less shall complete 14 hours of CE credit;\n\n(b) Individuals who have not held an active license for more than 3 months and less than 6 years shall complete the following CE credits;\n\n(1) Four CE credits of Occupational Safety and Health Association (OSHA) 29 CFR Part 1910 compliance training;\n\n(2) Four CE credits of bloodborne pathogen training;\n\n(3) Four CE credits of Federal Trade Commission (FTC) 16 CFR Part 453 compliance training; and\n\n(4) Four CE credits of current funeral and cremation trends; and\n\n(c) Individuals who have not held an active license for more than 6 years shall, in addition to the requirements set forth in (b) above, complete the following:\n\n(1) Pass a practical examination; and\n\n(2) Pass a written examination on the current state laws and rules governing the practice of funeral directing and embalming in the state of New Hampshire.\n\nSource. #6516, eff 5-24-97, EXPIRED: 5-24-05\n\nNew. #9387, eff 2-12-09 (from Frl 403.09); ss by #12129, eff 3-10-17; ss by #14645, eff 9-7-26, EXPIRES: 9-7-36 (formerly Frl 403.07)",
